WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.189
Let’s make a first purchase with Monsoon Table, our
example restaurant.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.332
Start with your restaurant’s name, contact number, and
address.

00:00:09.552 --> 00:00:13.414
Add your city, state and PIN code for the right
delivery details.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.324
Enter the owner’s name and work email.

00:00:22.544 --> 00:00:27.408
For approved pilot owners, continue with Google to
create the workspace and open Today.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.421
Open Menu, choose Add menu, then type or paste a dish.

00:00:35.641 --> 00:00:37.486
Here, we’re making tomato curry.

00:00:37.706 --> 00:00:40.096
Review the ingredient, quantity and unit.

00:00:40.316 --> 00:00:42.981
Approve the menu before using it for a purchase.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.118
Open Suppliers and add the businesses you buy from.

00:00:53.338 --> 00:00:56.450
Enter each business name and its ingredient
categories.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:00.425
We’ve added two example suppliers so we can compare
their replies.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.891
Choose New purchase. Give it a name and select the
approved menu.

00:01:10.111 --> 00:01:12.948
Check quantities. We need ten kilos of tomatoes.

00:01:13.168 --> 00:01:15.526
Set the delivery date and reply deadline.

00:01:15.746 --> 00:01:19.010
Choose your suppliers, save the draft, then open it
for quotes.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.822
Each supplier opens their private request link.

00:01:31.042 --> 00:01:34.775
They enter a price, check delivery and the total, then
send their quote.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.403
Here are replies from our two example suppliers, for
the same ten kilos.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.781
Back in Purchases, compare the complete offers.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.229
Check coverage, tax, delivery charges and dates.

00:01:52.449 --> 00:01:55.863
Here, the totals are four hundred and four hundred
forty rupees.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.901
Choose the suitable supplier and confirm your
decision.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.890
Now check what actually arrives.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.810
We ordered ten kilos, but received nine.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.099
Enter received quantities and check the invoice.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.402
Record the missing kilo and forty rupees in credit
still owed, then save.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.847
Return to Today. Your purchase and delivery follow-up
are visible.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.382
Your team can see what needs attention next.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.761
Ready to make your first purchase?

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.904
Start with pilot access, set up your restaurant, and
follow these steps.
